  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The correct option is <b>In the Properties section for the EC2 resource inside the Resources block</b>. When using AWS CloudFormation to configure EC2 instances, you must supply the <b>UserData</b> parameter within the <b>Properties</b> key of the EC2 instance under the <b>Resources</b> section. This field allows CloudFormation to inject the desired configuration script at instance launch.</p><p>Looking at the incorrect options:</p><ul><li><i>Within the Metadata section under Outputs for the EC2 instance</i>: The <i>Outputs</i> section is used for returning information from the stack, not for instance launch configuration or scripts.</li><li><i>Under the Metadata field of the EC2 instance in the Resources area</i>: Although the <i>Metadata</i> section can be used for additional resource data, it is not the place to configure <b>UserData</b> scripts for EC2 instance initialization; <b>UserData</b> works specifically within <b>Properties</b>.</li><li><i>Inside the Properties area for the EC2 instance inside the Outputs section</i>: There is no such structure in CloudFormation; <i>Outputs</i> is not designed to declare resources.</li></ul><p><b>Tip:</b> Always place <b>UserData</b> under <b>Properties</b> for the relevant EC2 resource in the <b>Resources</b> section. Familiarize yourself with the structure of a proper CloudFormation template for EC2 resources to easily spot errors or misplacements during exams.</p>",
  "query": "<p>You're creating a CloudFormation template to deploy web servers on EC2 instances. Where should you specify the UserData so it is correctly provided to the EC2 instances?</p>",
